# desktop — Agent Instructions

Read `packages/apps/desktop/CLAUDE.md` first. This is the Electron 40 shell.

## Key facts

- Runtime: strict TypeScript main/preload under `electron/`.
- Authority: machine bootstrap, source lifecycle, native windows and updates;
  never trading or broker writes.
- Origin: exact packaged splash file or selected `127.0.0.1` backend only.
- Background runtime: close hides to tray; explicit quit drains and stops the
  owned guardian containment.
- First launch: checksum-verified tools and frozen-lock source build under
  `~/.flinttrade/src/FlintTrade`.

## Working here

- Run `make desktop-test`, `make desktop-build`, and the relevant package smoke.
- Preserve the named `window.flintDesktop` bridge and per-handler sender
  validation; never add a generic IPC escape hatch.
- Keep the running checkout immutable. Source candidates use sibling paths and
  an isolated health workspace; user data never moves with source.
- Source/runtime and shell-installer updates remain separate operations.
- Conventional Commits use scope `desktop`.

## Verification

Local Electron TypeScript, Vitest, bundle and host package must be green when
their surfaces change. Windows/Linux package and process semantics require
deterministic tests plus CI/contributor runs; one Mac is not cross-platform
proof. Never push without explicit maintainer permission.
